<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark">
  <title>First-run setup · <%= siteName %></title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/platform-shell.css">
  <style>.setupSteps{display:flex;gap:8px;margin:14px 0 22px}.setupStep{font-size:12px;padding:6px 9px;border:1px solid #334155;border-radius:999px;color:#94a3b8}.setupStep.active{color:#fff;border-color:#64748b}.codeHint{font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;background:#0f172a;border:1px solid #334155;border-radius:10px;padding:12px;margin:14px 0;color:#cbd5e1;line-height:1.55}.codeHint code{user-select:all;color:#fff}.setupHelp{margin:10px 0 18px;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.55}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="authShell">
  <section class="authCard">
    <div class="authBrand"><%= siteName %></div>
    <div class="muted">Secure first-run installer</div>
    <div class="setupSteps"><span class="setupStep active">1 · Claim install</span><span class="setupStep">2 · Create admin</span><span class="setupStep">3 · Dashboard</span></div>
    <h1 class="authTitle">Claim this installation</h1>
    <p class="muted">A one-time setup code is required before the first administrator can be created. This prevents an internet visitor from claiming a newly deployed server.</p>
    <div class="setupHelp"><strong>You do not need to search application logs.</strong> On the server, from the CAPTAiNFiN compose directory, run the command below. It prints a fresh one-time code and invalidates any older code.</div>
    <div class="codeHint"><code>docker compose exec app npm run setup:claim</code></div>
    <p class="setupHelp">If the app container is not running yet, use <code>docker compose run --rm app npm run setup:claim</code> instead. Copy the code it prints into the field below.</p>
    <% if (error) { %><div class="notice error"><%= error %></div><% } %>
    <form method="post" action="/setup/claim" autocomplete="off">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
      <div class="formGroup">
        <label for="setupCode">One-time setup code</label>
        <input class="input" id="setupCode" name="setupCode" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" required autofocus>
      </div>
      <div class="buttonRow"><button class="button" type="submit">Continue securely</button></div>
    </form>
    <p class="securityNote">The setup endpoint permanently locks after the first native administrator is created.</p>
  </section>
</main>
</body>
</html>
